BT 1 0 0 1 0 50 Tm /F3 10 Tf 15 TL .037308 Tw (A companion to Part III and Part IV, prompted by Solzhenitsyn's long meditation on Article 58. Two things sit behind the Gulag: a criminal statute elastic enough) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.0044 Tw (to catch anyone, and an official philosophy that made the catching feel like historical necessity. This section lays out the statute section by section with the) Tj T* 0 Tw .0044 Tw (punishments it prescribed, shows how the OSO and its coded charges turned it into sentencing by the fileful, gives the archival numbers with an honest account) Tj T* 0 Tw (of what they can and cannot tell us, and then treats the dialectical doctrine \227 distinguishing carefully between what is documented and what is merely argued.) Tj T* ET
